 "posture": "Breadth reads 32.8/100 (Weakening; equity-exposure band 40–60%) and VIX at 26.62 just came off Friday's 35.89 panic peak after Monday's +4.7% S&P / +6.5% Nasdaq relief rally — but every major index is still below both its 50- and 200-day averages (S&P −7.4% from its 52-week high, Nasdaq-100 −14.3%). The rally's fuel was Jensen Huang's reinstatement as Nvidia CEO (NVDA +31.5%, best day in 20+ years) rather than a change in the macro setup: the Fed hiked in September, another hike is expected Dec 9, and the 10-year sits at 4.92%, so the 'good news' also revived rate-hike pricing and capped crypto's bounce. The AI-unwind correction is paused, not resolved — the peak/trough component (15/100) says breadth is past a peak and still declining, while only 11% of tracked alts sit above their 200-day average and the crypto regime scores 37.4/100 RISK_OFF. Treat rallies as suspect until breadth confirms; Wednesday's October PCE is the next binary catalyst, with Thanksgiving-week liquidity thin.",
